# Repository-wide ignores.
#
# Each app also has its own .gitignore (svv-balaji-admin, svv-balaji-backend,
# svv-balaji-field). This file is the backstop: a folder added later gets the
# important rules without anyone remembering to copy them, which is exactly what
# went wrong when svv-balaji-field was created without one and git offered to
# commit ten thousand files from node_modules.

# --- Dependencies and build output, anywhere in the tree -------------------
node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
build/
.vite/

# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Never commit a real .env - the backend's holds the database URL, the JWT
# secrets and the storage credentials. The .example files are the template and
# are committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Generated code --------------------------------------------------------
# The Prisma client is regenerated from schema.prisma by `npx prisma generate`
# on every machine. Committing it causes the exact "does not exist on type
# PrismaService" confusion it is meant to prevent.
.prisma/
generated/

# --- Logs, coverage, caches ------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
coverage/
.cache/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Editors and OS --------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Office lock and temp files --------------------------------------------
# LibreOffice and Excel leave these behind while a document is open. They are
# per-machine and change constantly.
.~lock.*#
~$*
*.tmp.pdf
*.xlsx#

# --- Local developer tooling -----------------------------------------------
# Per-developer state from AI coding assistants. The instruction files at the
# root (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, GEMINI.md and friends) ARE committed on purpose -
# they are shared project context. These directories are local caches and
# session state, which are not.
.claude/
.codebuddy/
.gemini/
.kiro/
.qoder/
.code-review-graph/

# --- Stray files that are not project sources ------------------------------
# Installer scripts, screenshots and pasted images. Delete them if they are not
# needed; ignoring keeps them out of the history either way.
get-pip.py
WhatsApp Image *.jpeg
WhatsApp Image *.jpg
branch_structure.json
temp_auto_push.bat
temp_interactive_push.bat
